# Where quote requests are delivered.
#
# Until QUOTE_TO is set, /api/quote logs the full submission and tells the
# visitor the truth. Nothing is lost, but nothing is delivered either, and the
# warning shows up in the Vercel log on every submission.
#
# Mail goes over SMTP through a mailbox the client already owns rather than a
# hosted API with its own subscription. If the agency has no mailbox yet, send
# from a glazedweb.com address with replyTo set to the customer, so client DNS
# work is never on the critical path.
#
# Kevin sets these in the Vercel dashboard. Never paste a secret into a file.

QUOTE_TO=
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM=

# Where the intake sheet at /intake is delivered: Kevin's inbox, over Resend
# from the verified glazedweb.com sending domain with a sending-only key for
# this project. This is studio mail, not client mail, which is why it is not
# on the SMTP rail above. Until both are set, /api/intake logs the full
# submission and warns.
INTAKE_TO=
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Payments. The checkout only takes a card once payments.checkoutEnabled in
# lib/site.ts is flipped on, and the flip conditions live on that flag: this
# must be HER Stripe account, settling into a premium/trust bank account, with
# her written go-ahead on the fee. Until then, pay links still show the bill
# and route carrier-billed policies to the carrier; they just cannot charge.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY        GLAZED'S platform key (sk_live_... or sk_test_...).
#                          A test key opens the checkout without the switch in
#                          site.ts, because it cannot move real money.
# STRIPE_ACCOUNT           her connected account (acct_...), from Glazed's
#                          Stripe > Connect after she finishes onboarding. The
#                          charge lands in her balance under her name, and the
#                          .99 goes to Glazed as an application fee at the
#                          moment of payment. Without it, calls run on the
#                          key's own account and no fee is split.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET    from Stripe > Developers > Webhooks, endpoint
#                          https://<host>/api/stripe/webhook with the events
#                          checkout.session.completed, invoice.paid,
#                          customer.subscription.deleted. Without it, one-time
#                          payments still record on the return page; autopay
#                          cycles record once it is set and Stripe replays.
# PAY_LINK_SECRET          signs the pay links. Any long random string. Unset
#                          in production means no pay links and no bill lookup
#                          (a closed door, not a known lock). Rotating it
#                          retires every link ever sent.
# PAY_NOTIFY_TO            where "payment received" notes land.
# CRON_SECRET              Vercel signs the nightly reminder call with it.
#                          Unset in production means the job sends nothing.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
PAY_LINK_SECRET=
PAY_NOTIFY_TO=
CRON_SECRET=

# The workroom at /workroom: the agency's leads queue, her book of customers
# and policies, the payments screen and the site-facts editor. Customer
# reminder emails go out over the RESEND_API_KEY above, from the studio's
# domain with reply-to set to her address, until she has a mailbox of her
# own (see the README).
#
# WORKROOM_PASSCODE guards customer contact details. Minimum 4 characters
# (was 8; lowered September 1, 2026 for a code she can keep in her head, with
# the login rate limiter tightened to match). Unset (or shorter) in production
# CLOSES the door rather than falling back to anything guessable.
WORKROOM_PASSCODE=
#
# Storage for leads and for the facts she edits. Vercel > Storage > Create
# Database > Neon sets this for you, and the tables create themselves on
# first use. The integration sometimes injects a PREFIXED name instead
# (SOMETHING_DATABASE_URL); the store finds any variable ending in
# _DATABASE_URL or _POSTGRES_URL, so nothing needs copying between rows.
# Without a database the workroom runs on in-memory storage, says so on
# screen, and the quote handler still logs every submission in full so
# nothing is lost.
DATABASE_URL=
